# HARNESS OUTPUT, NOT APPLICATION FILES (2026-10-08, measurement).
# Measured: `vercel dev` held 10,284 open descriptors against 10,229 files in the tree — about one
# per file — while failing intermittently with `spawn EBADF` (4 of 30 mocked requests served).
# These six directories are run artefacts the served app never reads. This file ALSO excludes them
# from deployment uploads, which is why it is being measured rather than assumed.
_fs_live_out/
_continuation_live_eval_out/
_fs_issue_corpus_out/
_audit_out/
_tempt_fate_fixtures/
_fs_planner_capture_out/

# SAME FAILURE MODE, RECURRED (2026-10-15, measured). `vercel dev` (PID 53947, --debug) held 10,264
# open descriptors against 10,222 project files — one per file, and within 20 of the 2026-10-08
# figures above — while every API route returned NO_RESPONSE_FROM_FUNCTION and the server trace
# showed `spawn EBADF` after the builder had already imported successfully.
#
# These two directories were not listed above and held 5,719 of those 10,222 descriptors (56%):
#   _ab_writing_out  3,019   ·   _validate_out  2,700
# Verified before adding: neither is referenced by public/, api/, package.json or vercel.json. Only
# harness .mjs scripts read them, from disk, which this file does not affect.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT: proof of the descriptor bug. The process was holding all 10,264 successfully,
# and EBADF ("bad descriptor") is not EMFILE ("none available") — so exhaustion was never
# demonstrated. This reduces a measured condition that accompanied the documented failure twice.
_ab_writing_out/
_validate_out/

# THIRD RECURRENCE (2026-10-30, measured). `vercel dev` (PID 55583) held 7,054 open descriptors,
# 7,031 of them REG files inside the project tree, on a process ~2 minutes old, while the console
# reported `spawn EBADF` and two OPENING_PLANNER requests to /api/proxy returned 502 with no
# `[SPECIALIST-PROXY]` line and no usage receipt.
#
# Descriptors by top-level directory at the time of measurement (the rest of the tree below these):
#   public 847 (legitimately served)   ·   _nf_fresh_continuation_out 605   ·   _nf_capture 560
#   _stage0_out 401   ·   _saydo_gibberish_out 353   ·   _nf_scaffold_control_out 131
#   _live_corpus_out 125   ·   _scene2_repair_replay_sample_out 110   ·   _nf_author_request_out 100
#   _nf_playthrough_out 90   ·   _nf_cg_delivery_out 72   ·   _quarantine 69
#
# Verified before adding, across api/, public/, scripts/, vercel.json, package.json and .githooks/:
# none is read by the served app. The only three matches anywhere are COMMENTS in public/app.js
# citing evidence paths (lines 8897, 9073, 322094) — nothing loads them at runtime, and vercel.json
# declares no includeFiles. Harness .mjs scripts read them from disk, which this file does not
# affect. Listed explicitly rather than as `_nf_*` so a future harness directory is a deliberate
# addition and not silently excluded from deployment.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT, restated because it has now been tempting three times: this is mitigation of a
# measured watched-file load that ACCOMPANIED the failure, not a confirmed fix. EBADF is still
# "bad descriptor", not EMFILE "none available", so exhaustion remains undemonstrated; file CHURN
# (harnesses deleting and recreating output directories inside the watched tree) fits the error
# name at least as well. It is NOT established that EBADF produced the two planner 502s: the
# process that served them was restarted before it could be inspected, and a missing
# `[SPECIALIST-PROXY]` line does not by itself prove the handler never executed.
_nf_fresh_continuation_out/
_nf_capture/
_stage0_out/
_saydo_gibberish_out/
_nf_scaffold_control_out/
_live_corpus_out/
_scene2_repair_replay_sample_out/
_nf_author_request_out/
_nf_playthrough_out/
_nf_cg_delivery_out/
_quarantine/

# ── NEVER UPLOAD A LOCAL ENV FILE OR ITS BACKUPS (Roman 2026-11-15) ──────────────────────────
# `.env.local` is gitignored and so never deployed, but `.env.local.bak-20261108` is NOT, and a
# preview deploy would have carried 34 API keys into the deployment's own filesystem. Secrets
# reach a deployment through the project's configured environment variables, never through a file
# in the upload. Checked before the first preview deploy, not after.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.*

# ── TEST OUTPUT DIRECTORIES ARE NEVER DEPLOYED (Roman 2026-11-15) ────────────────────────────
# Each run directory carries a `LATEST` symlink to an absolute local path, which the build
# container rejects outright: "/vercel/path0/_ft_arrival_probe/LATEST is not a valid symlink"
# failed the first preview deploy. There are 66 such directories. They are harness artefacts and
# have no business in a deployment regardless.
_ft_*/
_nf_*/
_ab_writing_out/
_audit_out/
_canon_audit_selective_out/
_cg_ground_truth_census_out/
_validate_out/
_fs_live_out/

# The symlink itself, by name, wherever it appears — the directory patterns above did not
# reliably exclude every run folder and the build container rejects the symlink, not the folder.
**/LATEST
LATEST
